Author: Moritz Hoffmann <antiguru@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 1 02:23:15 2026 +0200

    Add the base/expressions assertion-table harness (Task 15, consuming half)
    
    rexx-exec/tests/assertions.rs runs every AssertionRow rexx-extract's
    extract_assertions lifts out of ootest/ooRexx/base/expressions/ through
    rexx_exec's public entry point, comparing byte for byte rather than
    numerically so the created-digits/created-form rendering story (D15) can't
    hide behind a numeric equality. Two falsification proofs (value rows and
    raise-expectation rows) confirm the table can actually fail; a third test
    confirms it is sensitive to each row's own carried NUMERIC DIGITS/FORM
    rather than a shared default.
    
    Running the harness for real found a second extractor modeling gap beyond
    the CONCATENATION prelude trap 15a already caught: self~expectSyntax defers
    a raise-check to a later statement in the same method, so a self~assertSame
    that follows one is not testing "expr equals expected", it's testing
    "evaluating expr raises major.sub" -- 184 of 4,259 extracted rows were
    mis-modeled as value comparisons. Fixed in rexx-extract by converting those
    rows (AssertionRow::expect_raise, carried sequentially like digits/form)
    rather than dropping them, since they are the table's only coverage of the
    raise path; self~assertSyntaxError/assertRuntimeError check their own raise
    inline and don't defer, so they're left alone, and self~expectCondition
    (a named, non-numeric condition) blocks rather than being silently
    mismodeled the same way.
    
    Measured result: 4,224 of 4,259 rows pass. The remaining 35 are genuine
    runtime gaps, all in Literals.testGroup, named and attributed to their
    owning sub-phase (33 message sends, Phase 5; 2 function calls, 4b) rather
    than folded into an unattributed blocked bucket.
    
